   "design": "Students check in at studio by scanning the session code, jury members score on an online rubric form that averages per project, and students upload final boards to the course archive in a fixed format; final grades sync from the gradebook to the student records system after the teacher confirms. The teacher no longer types sign-in sheets, copies jury sheets, re-enters grades or collects and renames files. Entering final grades, arrangements, administration questions and the exam board stay with the teacher as examiner.",
   "previous_blocker": "Attendance, jury scores, grades and boards were copied by hand between paper, mail and two systems.",
   "enabler_now": "Code check-in, online jury forms, archive uploads and a gradebook sync.",
   "still_hard": "External jurors who will not use the form.",
   "human_edge": "Handling a student's special arrangement fairly.",
