   "design": "Questions and tagged building images live in an item bank from which the paper is assembled. The exam runs in a digital test platform that marks image identification and calculation items against the key with item statistics. Theory essays are grouped by argument so the teacher marks each group once and reads every answer; no model proposes marks. The platform adds up sections. Writing questions, colleague review, invigilation, marking, entering grades and the inspection session stay with the teacher as examiner.",
   "previous_blocker": "Image sheets were laid out and closed items marked and totalled by hand.",
   "enabler_now": "Item banks with images, digital closed-item marking and answer grouping.",
   "still_hard": "Hand-drawn sketch answers.",
   "human_edge": "Judging whether a student understands why a building works.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Less marking and totalling; examiner judgement stays.",
